# /sdlc-gates

Run `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc gates` (on Windows PowerShell or cmd: `.\<%sdlcDir%>\sdlc.cmd gates`). These are the checks that do not need the running system, so they are the fast feedback.
Give the command up to 10 minutes.

- Report one line per gate: its id, PASS or FAIL, and the time. Then the verdict.
- A gate failed: show the first lines of its log (the report names the path under `.ai/evidence/`) and say in a sentence what is wrong.
  This command only reports: do not change any file unless the person asks you to.
- To check just one gate again: `./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc gates --only <gate-id>`. The facts against the running system are `/sdlc-verify`.
